  "notes": "Rock-songwriting craft applied to Latin-pop crossover, windowed to 1990+ as the research does, which clears Gate 2. 96–140 straight with the backbeat on 2&4. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick on 1 and the '&' of 2 in a **tumbao-derived** placement\" (a high `tresilloBias` with the second anchor on \"2&\"), \"16th timbale rim figures\" — which is why the perc block is timbale- and rim-led rather than conga-led, the clearest separation from the Ricky Martin artist entry that shares the flagship record — and \"a percussion break is used in place of a drum fill\", so the fills are pushed to 8 and 16 bars while the percussion density stays high. The bass rule is documented and encoded literally: \"played bass locked to the kick with an **anticipated bass note on the '&' of 4** (Latin anticipated-bass habit) and octave leaps under brass hits\", i.e. `mirror_kick` with `anticipationProb` at 0.62 and the octave as a passing tone. Harmony is i–VII–VI–VII and i–iv–V vamps with brass and guitar riffs \"harmonised in 4ths/5ths above the tonic triad\", and his craft signature is the arena title hook \"placed on beats 1–2 of the chorus\" over a shouted three-note cell rather than a melodic arc — hence the low motif pitch count and the call-and-response structure. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and says the general habits are inferred across the catalogue. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 122.",
